  "number": 5903,
  "title": "Don't announce a single audio, video, or animation in a card as a list item",
  "body": "> Fixes #5722\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed screen readers announcing a single audio, video, or animation in a card as a list item, such as \"1 of 1\", fixes [#5722](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/issues/5722), in PR [#5903](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/5903), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\nAudio, video, and animation cards always rendered their media as a `<ul>` with one `<li>` per medium, so screen readers announced the only player of a card as a list item, \"1 of 1\". Media are now marked up as a list only when there are 2 or more; a single medium is wrapped in `<div>` elements with the same class and looks the same. This also removes the list from the scan-mode reading in #5736.\n\n## Design\n\n- Decision: the `media-list` class is kept, but host CSS that targets `ul.media-list` or its `li` no longer matches a single medium.\n- Open question: would you rather keep `<ul>`/`<li>` with `role=\"none\"` for a single medium, so the DOM does not change?\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `MediaList` (new, internal to the bundle): renders `ul > li` for 2 or more media, otherwise `div > div`\n- `AudioCardContent`, `VideoCardContent`, `AnimationCardContent`: render their media with `MediaList`; their styles select `.media-list` and its children instead of `ul.media-list` and `li`\n- `SignInCardContent.module.css`: removed an unused `ul.media-list` rule (sign-in cards have no media)\n- `testHelpers.getAccessibilityAncestors` (new): the ancestors of an element in the accessibility tree\n- Added `richCard/mediaCard.mediaList.html`: audio, video, and animation cards with a single medium are not in a list, and an audio card with 2 media is a list of 2\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [x] I have updated `CHANGELOG.md`\n- [ ] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
